1
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:18,009
(GBRB: Farm Operation - Go Go Farm)

2
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:20,609
(Lee Kwang Soo)

3
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:22,709
(Kim Woo Bin)

4
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:24,949
(Doh Kyung Soo)

5
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:28,050
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

6
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:31,860
(GBRB: Farm Operation - Go Go Farm)

7
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:34,320
Honestly, if he tells me to get flat on the ground, I will.

8
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,289
(Go away.)

9
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:38,159
(Kwang Soo and John Snow can't seem to get along.)

10
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,559
- Could you switch with me?
- Sure.

11
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,069
Thank you. Let's go, Yeonjin.

12
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:43,629
(Eventually, he's assigned to a new partner, Yeonjin.)

13
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:46,370
(He makes his secondhand marketplace username to Yeonjin's Dad.)

14
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:50,809
(They post a listing to sell compost made from horse manure.)

15
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:53,740
(Then a mysterious visitor shows up at KKPP.)

16
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:57,819
(A bright-eyed new intern makes an appearance.)

17
00:00:57,820 --> 00:01:00,750
(Actress Shin Ye Eun, young Yeon Jin from "The Glory")

18
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:02,919
We can assign Yeonjin to her.

19
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:05,219
(Kwang Soo, your partner is John Snow.)

20
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:07,960
(The real Yeon Jin showed up and stole his partner away.)

21
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:13,560
(Paired with Yeonjin, Ye Eun heads out to the field.)

22
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,430
Yeonjin, have some grass.

23
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:17,070
It's time to graze.

24
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:19,840
I'll let you graze.

25
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:21,869
(He refuses and goes back.)

26
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:23,570
(Being dragged)

27
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:26,380
You can't run all of a sudden. No.

28
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:28,450
No!

29
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:30,710
(Screaming)

30
00:01:30,711 --> 00:01:31,820
Please stop him.

31
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:38,220
(For some reason, Yeonjin makes a run for it.)

32
00:01:38,990 --> 00:01:40,490
Gosh, he's really fast.

33
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:42,660
Park Yeonjin!

34
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,700
(Yeonjin's Dad goes after the runaway Yeonjin.)

35
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,870
(Yeonjin reaches a dead end.)

36
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:51,739
(Blocking the escape route)

37
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:52,900
He's trying to go in.

38
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:57,879
(Yeonjin is caught in no time.)

39
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,010
Why did you do that?

40
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:00,810
Calm down.

41
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:04,480
I felt like I'd get dragged along.

42
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:07,180
I don't think I can handle it.

43
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,750
(The intern is overwhelmed by this new experience.)

44
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,520
Did I hold the rope wrong?

45
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:14,140
When a horse decides to pull, there's not much you can do.

46
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,729
(Neighing)

47
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:17,359
- Hey, what's wrong?
- He's angry.

48
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,660
You've got quite the personality.

49
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,899
Why are you in a bad mood?

50
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,820
(He tries to calm him down with a gentle touch.)

51
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,270
(Pushing away)

52
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:29,969
(Stumbling)

53
00:02:29,970 --> 00:02:31,339
Does he like it or not?

54
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:32,380
I don't know.

55
00:02:32,710 --> 00:02:35,050
(No one can figure out what's on Yeonjin's mind.)

56
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:37,080
Eat some grass here.

57
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,720
Hey.

58
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,090
(He doesn't show interest in grazing.)

59
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:45,659
(Neighing loudly)

60
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:47,730
What's the matter? No.

61
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,460
Achick.

62
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:53,560
(He's especially stubborn today.)

63
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,569
It's impossible to handle him.

64
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:57,700
Achick.

65
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,500
(When he really refuses to cooperate...)

66
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:00,700
Sung Joon.

67
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:02,910
Sung Joon.

68
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:06,240
No, wait. You must wait.

69
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:08,810
Yeonjin, wait.

70
00:03:09,510 --> 00:03:10,550
No.

71
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:12,220
Don't push me.

72
00:03:14,350 --> 00:03:16,250
(Just then, Sung Joon arrives.)

73
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:17,490
Don't push me.

74
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,659
(Here you go.)

75
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,660
Nope!

76
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:25,030
(The situation is under control after one word.)

77
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,429
(Kwang Soo is silent.)

78
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:28,600
You have to be firm with him.

79
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,540
(Kwang Soo goes back after being rejected by Yeonjin.)

80
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:36,669
(Afternoon task, grooming)

81
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:39,040
Now it's time to wash the horses.

82
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,480
- Kwang Soo.
- Yes?

83
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,609
Hurry up and bring your partner horse.

84
00:03:43,610 --> 00:03:45,280
- Which one?
- Snow.

85
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:46,949
Where's Snow?

86
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:47,989
(My partner Snow?)

87
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:49,120
- John Snow.
- Where's Snow?

88
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,519
- Is this Snow?
- Yes.

89
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,760
He got bigger than before.

90
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,960
Just in one day... Is this really Snow?

91
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,359
(He was in front of him, but he completely missed him.)

92
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,400
Do I bring him?

93
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:01,329
Let's go.

94
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:02,770
(The ex-partner comes to take Snow.)

95
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:04,700
Achick.

96
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,940
(They head over to the grooming area.)

97
00:04:09,070 --> 00:04:10,139
Kwang Soo, please go in first.

98
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:11,140
- Do we go in?
- Yes.

99
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,210
(Grooming removes dirt...)

100
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:14,309
(trapped in the horse's winter coat...)

101
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:15,449
(and helps prevent skin disease.)

102
00:04:15,450 --> 00:04:16,609
He's neighing.

103
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:17,619
It's because it's unfamiliar.

104
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:18,850
Please bring Yeonjin.

105
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:21,320
- Okay.
- Bring Yeonjin with you.

106
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,620
(It's time for Ye Eun to bring Yeonjin.)

107
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,040
Ye Eun, will you not take care of Yeonjin?

108
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:29,830
Are you going to wash Snow?

109
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:31,600
Tell me clearly.

110
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:33,500
(His love for Yeonjin starts again.)

111
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,330
No, I'll take care of Yeonjin.

112
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:39,100
(An unexpected battle over Yeonjin begins.)

113
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,270
Let's go.

114
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,110
Follow me.

115
00:04:46,710 --> 00:04:48,349
(Yeon Jin claims Yeonjin.)

116
00:04:48,350 --> 00:04:49,950
(He's still not ready to let go.)

117
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:52,880
(Neighing)

118
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,279
(Moaning)

119
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:56,119
- That startled me.
- Nope!

120
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,289
It startled me.

121
00:04:57,290 --> 00:04:59,390
(He sneaks his hand on the rope.)

122
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:03,160
(At last, Yeonjin also arrives at the grooming area.)

123
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:06,060
(The washer is on.)

124
00:05:06,830 --> 00:05:08,570
(His ears perk up.)

125
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,070
He seems interested.

126
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:14,070
They're basically large, medium, and small.

127
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:15,839
(Large John Snow)

128
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,009
(Medium Morris)

129
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:18,039
(Small Yeonjin)

130
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,086
(The partner horses are in clearly different sizes.)

131
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:23,609
You need to build a strong bond with your horse.

132
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:25,380
With our partner horse? Okay.

133
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,119
(He sneaks back towards Yeonjin again.)

134
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,120
Okay.

135
00:05:29,121 --> 00:05:30,820
Your horse is over there. Go to the front.

136
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:31,990
What?

137
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:33,659
- Yeonjin is my partner.
- What?

138
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:35,129
- Go to the front.
- My partner is Yeonjin...

139
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:36,289
Isn't he my partner?

140
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:37,629
Come on. Move to the front.

141
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,660
He's too big for me.

142
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,259
It's because yesterday...

143
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,929
There are rules for this.

144
00:05:41,930 --> 00:05:42,930
- Really?
- Snow is your partner.

145
00:05:42,931 --> 00:05:44,600
Then it'll be the opposite.

146
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:45,900
- Why do I...
- That's...

147
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:46,900
- Go.
- Okay.

148
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,470
(Kwang Soo ends up going back to Snow.)

149
00:05:50,670 --> 00:05:52,479
Can I spray water on him?

150
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,839
Spray some water on him.

151
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:55,080
(The grooming starts.)

152
00:05:55,580 --> 00:06:00,180
(Step 1: Start by wetting the parts farthest from the heart.)

153
00:06:01,450 --> 00:06:02,519
I squeezed out too much.

154
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,850
Yeonjin, I'll cool you off.

155
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:08,390
(Step 2: Wash the horse with horse shampoo.)

156
00:06:09,290 --> 00:06:11,130
Hey, you have to be nice to me.

157
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:12,530
Look how much effort...

158
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:15,570
I'm putting into taking care of you.

159
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:16,700
Isn't it refreshing?

160
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:21,770
(Meanwhile, Kyung Soo quietly brushes along the grain.)

161
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:25,680
Morris.

162
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:27,980
It's okay.

163
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:29,680
It will be over soon.

164
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,780
(Keeping a close eye on Morris's mood)

165
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:34,590
(How about Kwang Soo and John Snow?)

166
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,490
It's refreshing.

167
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:39,560
It's refreshing.

168
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,690
(John Snow is quiet.)

169
00:06:42,990 --> 00:06:44,959
It's refreshing.

170
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:46,720
(He's walking on eggshells for some reason.)

171
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:50,530
Gosh, it's refreshing.

172
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:53,700
(He's trying to win him back.)

173
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:56,570
They all look like ticks.

174
00:06:57,810 --> 00:06:59,140
One just fell off.

175
00:06:59,910 --> 00:07:02,010
I removed the ones that were on him with the brush.

176
00:07:02,450 --> 00:07:04,149
They were huge from sucking blood.

177
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:05,280
- Really?
- Yes.

178
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:07,680
I need to wash your hair.

179
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:11,490
(His secret weapon to win him over is...)

180
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:16,789
(The mane hair treatment begins.)

181
00:07:16,790 --> 00:07:19,529
You look like a hairstylist in Cheongdam-dong.

182
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:21,210
(Hands of a hairstylist in Cheongdam-dong)

183
00:07:24,030 --> 00:07:27,170
(With the meticulous touch of a true master)

184
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:31,680
(Treating him to the full premium grooming experience)

185
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:34,510
Doesn't it feel good?

186
00:07:36,010 --> 00:07:37,610
(Advancing one step)

187
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:39,880
He moves forward on his own.

188
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:42,219
He moves on his own.

189
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,596
(They look much closer than before.)

190
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,620
(Chuckling)

191
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:47,910
Are you scratching yourself?

192
00:07:48,330 --> 00:07:51,500
Dogs also kick their legs when you scratch their backs.

193
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:55,170
(Brushing away while imagining how clean he'll look)

194
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:57,999
(How are the Yeonjins doing?)

195
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,670
Your hair is very long.

196
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:02,010
(They come face-to-face for the first time.)

197
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:04,839
I'll wash your face too. Come here.

198
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,010
What's with your bangs?

199
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,510
Your bangs look funny.

200
00:08:08,810 --> 00:08:10,910
Let's clean between your eyes too.

201
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:12,520
Now it's nice and clean.

202
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:15,989
The dirty water keeps coming.

203
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:17,550
(Years of grime finally come to light.)

204
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,920
(Getting an entirely new look)

205
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,160
Let's wash your backside too.

206
00:08:23,330 --> 00:08:25,730
That must be so refreshing.

207
00:08:29,670 --> 00:08:31,130
Kyung Soo, you're doing a good job.

208
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:35,440
(Carefully checking to see if there's any missed spot)

209
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:37,110
It's over.

210
00:08:37,770 --> 00:08:40,610
(Thanks to their perfect teamwork, they're first to finish shampooing.)

211
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:43,610
(The grooming session is almost done.)

212
00:08:44,450 --> 00:08:47,580
(Step 3: Rinse off the remaining shampoo.)

213
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:55,190
(Morris's coat looks noticeably brighter.)

214
00:08:56,130 --> 00:08:58,400
(Feeling fresh)

215
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:02,730
(Once every last bit of shampoo is rinsed away)

216
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:07,669
(Step 4: Dry off the excess water.)

217
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:09,790
Yeonjin, I didn't realize you had white in your coat.

218
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:13,280
(Sparkling clean Yeonjin is born again.)

219
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:15,910
Give some carrots to the horses.

220
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,080
Carrots.

221
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,350
It must be delicious.

222
00:09:21,590 --> 00:09:23,890
(A carrot reward for their partner's hard work)

223
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:26,890
(The afternoon grooming session comes to an end.)

224
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:31,030
(How was this afternoon's training?)

225
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:32,760
This is Kwang Snow.

226
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,080
I decided to adopt him into my family.

227
00:09:36,430 --> 00:09:40,170
If Snow ever wants to live as a human,

228
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:42,180
I'd be willing to become a horse instead.

229
00:09:42,670 --> 00:09:44,140
I didn't just wash him.

230
00:09:45,610 --> 00:09:48,850
We put on a whole performance together.

231
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,150
That's right.

232
00:09:51,151 --> 00:09:54,049
(He's in love with John Snow.)

233
00:09:54,050 --> 00:09:55,450
He gave me the least trouble,

234
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,020
and he listened the best.

235
00:09:57,820 --> 00:10:00,020
I feel like Morris and I have grown closer,

236
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:02,290
but I don't know if he feels the same.

237
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:06,400
I poured all my focus into cleaning his coat.

238
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:11,230
I think I cleaned him even better than I clean myself.

239
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,340
After washing him,

240
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,710
he seemed a little more obedient.

241
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,240
Now...

242
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:20,010
I just got you cleaned up. You can't dig in the dirt.

243
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,150
Watch.

244
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:24,779
Haven't you gotten mature?

245
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:26,740
(Do you know how hard I worked to get you clean?)

246
00:10:27,350 --> 00:10:28,420
Stop!

247
00:10:29,990 --> 00:10:30,990
We still got closer.

248
00:10:30,991 --> 00:10:32,989
He used to push me away when I approached him,

249
00:10:32,990 --> 00:10:34,460
but now, he stays still.

250
00:10:35,890 --> 00:10:38,700
(Undaunted, he keeps digging.)

251
00:10:39,330 --> 00:10:40,459
More than I thought...

252
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:42,530
Gosh, no.

253
00:10:42,970 --> 00:10:44,600
It finally started.

254
00:10:45,370 --> 00:10:46,600
No.

255
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,410
(I refuse to watch.)

256
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:53,140
Don't shake it off.

257
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,750
She washed him...

258
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,320
But why...

259
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:03,320
Try to stop him.

260
00:11:04,650 --> 00:11:06,119
(Ye Eun is quiet.)

261
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,560
There's no use stopping him. Leave him be.

262
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:09,990
It's his life anyway.

263
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:15,170
You really know how to live life.

264
00:11:16,670 --> 00:11:19,570
If he's doing it because he's happy, I guess that's a good thing.

265
00:11:19,770 --> 00:11:22,310
(Yeonjin is being Yeonjin again today.)

266
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:26,479
(GBRB: Farm Operation - Go Go Farm)

267
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:29,049
(Lee Kwang Soo)

268
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:31,279
(Kim Woo Bin)

269
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:33,480
(Doh Kyung Soo)

270
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:40,360
(GBRB: Farm Operation - Go Go Farm)

271
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,330
The raw fish restaurant is huge.

272
00:11:42,730 --> 00:11:43,759
I know.

273
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,799
It will be delicious. I haven't smelled this in a long time.

274
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,459
- The smell...
- Of a raw fish restaurant?

275
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:48,470
Right.

276
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:50,700
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

277
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:53,669
- Hello.
- Hello.

278
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:54,670
How are you?

279
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,009
Don't do that.

280
00:11:56,010 --> 00:11:57,240
- What?
- Today...

281
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:59,479
- Did you hear about that?
- About what?

282
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:01,550
Today...

283
00:12:02,210 --> 00:12:03,279
After the meal...

284
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,349
(Tonight's team dinner comes with a special event.)

285
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:05,520
For the tab...

286
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:08,620
It will be the production crew versus us.

287
00:12:08,890 --> 00:12:10,550
The losing team picks up the tab.

288
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:12,519
(A team dinner with the bill on the line)

289
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,789
We'll eat first.

290
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:15,429
If we do it before dinner,

291
00:12:15,430 --> 00:12:17,290
- things might get awkward.
- Right.

292
00:12:17,490 --> 00:12:20,459
We'll make it simple. It will be either KKPP Food...

293
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,969
or egg is coming.

294
00:12:21,970 --> 00:12:25,839
The horse protection center team will split into two sides.

295
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:27,599
Then why don't we do this?

296
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:30,610
The CEO of KKPP Food can cover...

297
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:33,780
all the expenses...

298
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,620
- What?
- What are you talking about?

299
00:12:36,210 --> 00:12:38,550
What are you talking about? I'm not even the real CEO.

300
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,780
Aren't you the CEO?

301
00:12:41,790 --> 00:12:44,150
You always say that you're the CEO.

302
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,190
That's all fictional. What are you saying?

303
00:12:47,890 --> 00:12:48,989
(Reality hits when the dinner bill is on the line.)

304
00:12:48,990 --> 00:12:50,859
- Let's just do it.
- Let's eat first.

305
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:53,759
- Why don't we order...
- Let's enjoy some food first.

306
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,529
Do they only have course meals? No, right?

307
00:12:55,530 --> 00:12:56,530
There are things like this.

308
00:12:56,531 --> 00:12:59,269
- What do you like to eat?
- Isn't this a better choice?

309
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:00,769
- I like raw fish.
- Raw fish?

310
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:01,770
Let's order this.

311
00:13:01,771 --> 00:13:03,116
(They keep it simple and order a raw fish platter.)

312
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:04,140
By the way...

313
00:13:04,470 --> 00:13:07,440
Wait, I'll be honest.

314
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:11,679
I'd happily pay the bill with gratitude,

315
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:12,780
but isn't it too much?

316
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,749
I mean...

317
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:15,889
- I see.
- What I mean is...

318
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:18,289
Jun Wi, is it okay if we lose the bet?

319
00:13:18,290 --> 00:13:21,590
It'd definitely be nice if we won.

320
00:13:21,790 --> 00:13:24,029
You didn't tell me about it beforehand.

321
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:25,259
(He is also flustered.)

322
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,460
It's a little...

323
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:28,770
- Shall we call CEO Ko?
- Let's call...

324
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,799
CEO Ko first.

325
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,469
- Call CEO Ko?
- Can we call him?

326
00:13:33,470 --> 00:13:35,140
You mean, Joong Seok?

327
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:37,340
I'll call him.

328
00:13:38,070 --> 00:13:39,679
I will call him.

329
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,880
We should do that.

330
00:13:41,850 --> 00:13:43,179
(CEO Ko)

331
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,619
- Hello?
- Hello, CEO Ko.

332
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:47,280
This is CEO Lee from KKPP Food.

333
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:49,190
What are you doing?

334
00:13:49,690 --> 00:13:51,219
- I'm working.
- I see.

335
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:53,419
- We were also working.
- Right.

336
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,329
To wrap up...

337
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:57,729
- this season, - Yes.

338
00:13:57,730 --> 00:13:59,830
We wanted to have a team dinner as our wrap party.

339
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,169
- Okay.
- That's our plan.

340
00:14:02,170 --> 00:14:03,699
Everyone worked very hard...

341
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,499
- especially with the rain today.
- Right.

342
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,739
- I heard that it rained in Jeju.
- Yes.

343
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:10,969
- We're at a raw fish restaurant.
- Okay.

344
00:14:10,970 --> 00:14:14,680
With the full course meal,

345
00:14:15,380 --> 00:14:18,379
the bill might come out to around 2,500 dollars.

346
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:19,380
- However, - Yes.

347
00:14:19,381 --> 00:14:22,549
I'm not sure if KKPP Food can...

348
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:25,460
afford that amount.

349
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,219
That's what I'm worried about.

350
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:29,359
(Upset)

351
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,760
Sir, I'm Lee Kwang Soo.

352
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,760
Sir, I sang "Growl."

353
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:37,670
- Sir.
- Sir.

354
00:14:37,730 --> 00:14:40,670
- The member of EXO is growling.
- What?

355
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:43,610
I'm a huge fan of Doh Kyung Soo.

356
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:45,280
All of a sudden?

357
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:47,609
- Also, - Yes?

358
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:49,449
Ye Eun is with us.

359
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:51,409
- I'll put her on the phone.
- Shin Ye Eun.

360
00:14:51,410 --> 00:14:53,080
Shin Ye Eun is our intern.

361
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,449
- She's our new intern.
- Okay.

362
00:14:55,450 --> 00:14:56,450
(Taking a moment to introduce the intern)

363
00:14:56,451 --> 00:14:57,889
CEO Ko.

364
00:14:57,890 --> 00:14:59,559
- Hello.
- This is...

365
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,220
the new intern.

366
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:02,690
I see.

367
00:15:02,691 --> 00:15:04,259
(Laughing)

368
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:08,000
(Speechless)

369
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,569
Thank you for the food.

370
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:11,969
You're welcome, but we're going to win.

371
00:15:11,970 --> 00:15:13,239
No, we're going to win.

372
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:15,510
- All right.
- Okay.

373
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:17,870
- Sir, I'll call you again.
- Okay.

374
00:15:18,310 --> 00:15:19,779
Ye Eun also gets formal...

375
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:22,550
when she's on the phone with the CEO.

376
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:24,450
- She knows how to play along.
- Yes.

377
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:27,050
You don't use Jeju dialect at all.

378
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:29,350
I only use it sometimes...

379
00:15:29,690 --> 00:15:30,690
when I'm with my friends.

380
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:33,790
(He immediately goes quiet.)

381
00:15:33,990 --> 00:15:34,990
You know what?

382
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:37,929
Maybe he expresses himself differently,

383
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:39,850
but it feels like having something stuck inside.

384
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:42,230
Instead of being refreshing...

385
00:15:42,870 --> 00:15:43,870
It feels like...

386
00:15:44,430 --> 00:15:46,170
he can't fully let it out.

387
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:49,010
(Senior Sung Joon is the quiet type.)

388
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:51,569
Since he is your employee,

389
00:15:51,570 --> 00:15:54,480
can you tell us more about Sung Joon?

390
00:15:54,610 --> 00:15:57,810
He's been working with me for six months now.

391
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,949
I thought it's been much longer.

392
00:15:59,950 --> 00:16:01,470
- Me too.
- For the last six months...

393
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:04,550
One day, I got a message from him.

394
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:07,059
- When you didn't know each other?
- Right.

395
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:08,629
He wrote, "I'm a young man..."

396
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:11,960
"who wants to learn about horses from a horse ranch owner."

397
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:13,559
My response was,

398
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:16,170
"If you want to learn, come on over."

399
00:16:16,430 --> 00:16:18,800
He asked me what time he should come.

400
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:22,339
I couldn't tell him a specific time.

401
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:25,910
I said, "I always start work before sunrise."

402
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:29,409
I was sleeping in the ranch caravan.

403
00:16:29,410 --> 00:16:31,280
When I came outside,

404
00:16:31,850 --> 00:16:33,249
Sung Joon was waiting for me.

405
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,619
- Really?
- Gosh.

406
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,920
He arrived early in the morning.

407
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,090
That's how we started working together.

408
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,860
Now...

409
00:16:40,690 --> 00:16:43,959
I can't choose his future for him.

410
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:46,429
If he truly loves horses, I'd like to entrust...

411
00:16:46,430 --> 00:16:49,399
Sung Joon with every horse-related part of my ranch.

412
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,869
- By the way, - As my successor...

413
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:53,439
we asked about Sung Joon's strengths.

414
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,339
(The conversation took an unexpected detour.)

415
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,269
- What are his strengths?
- His strengths?

416
00:16:57,270 --> 00:16:58,939
He quietly endures the work.

417
00:16:58,940 --> 00:17:00,240
He has the kind of silence...

418
00:17:01,010 --> 00:17:02,010
that I don't have.

419
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:04,710
He really doesn't have that quiet side.

420
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:07,320
(Embarrassed)

421
00:17:07,450 --> 00:17:08,450
The food is here.

422
00:17:09,850 --> 00:17:10,950
It's starting.

423
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,090
It looks so good.

424
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,530
Enjoy your food.

425
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:16,989
Bon appetit.

426
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:18,110
Jun Wi, thanks for the food.

427
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,029
- Thank you.
- Thank you for the food.

428
00:17:20,030 --> 00:17:21,399
Thank you for the food.

429
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:23,270
(The tension begins before the first bite.)

430
00:17:23,470 --> 00:17:26,870
Do you like to eat it with soy sauce, sesame oil, ssamjang,

431
00:17:27,370 --> 00:17:28,869
or chojang?

432
00:17:28,870 --> 00:17:30,069
I usually eat it with chojang, but...

433
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:32,610
- Since it's your first bite...
- Right.

434
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:36,810
(To keep it light today, he eats it with soy sauce.)

435
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:40,319
So this is it.

436
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,320
(It melts in the mouth.)

437
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:45,860
It's very delicious.

438
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,730
It's my first time paying for raw fish.

439
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:51,389
- What?
- Really?

440
00:17:51,390 --> 00:17:52,929
It's his first time paying for raw fish.

441
00:17:52,930 --> 00:17:54,060
Seriously?

442
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,499
(He takes a bite quietly...)

443
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:59,700
(and savors the flavor in silence.)

444
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:06,580
Sir, did you get a message at the secondhand marketplace?

445
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,680
I did.

446
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,656
- Why isn't anyone contacting us?
- Why isn't anyone contacting us?

447
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:14,419
(The mysterious customer disappeared after leaving "1.")

448
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:16,989
I deleted the post and uploaded it again,

449
00:18:16,990 --> 00:18:19,059
and it got quite a few views.

450
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:20,859
It got 32 views.

451
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,230
- Thirty-two?
- Yes.

452
00:18:23,430 --> 00:18:25,199
Thirty-two people read it,

453
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:27,799
but no one has contacted us yet.

454
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,569
Why aren't we getting any inquiries?

455
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:30,570
(Discouraged)

456
00:18:30,630 --> 00:18:32,430
Sung Joon, didn't you get any compost orders?

457
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,610
You didn't get any orders?

458
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:37,569
I got an order of six bags.

459
00:18:37,570 --> 00:18:39,439
When? You got an order of six bags?

460
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,680
I got it before coming here,

461
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:43,550
but I told them to come next time because I didn't have time.

462
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,979
- Do you have proof?
- Show him the message.

463
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:46,980
It's because...

464
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:47,980
(Jealous of the huge gap in their secondhand business)

465
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:50,350
It should be...

466
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:53,260
Kyung Soo.

467
00:18:54,390 --> 00:18:56,190
- My daughter is calling me.
- Hand it to me.

468
00:18:57,230 --> 00:18:58,230
I'll pick up.

469
00:18:58,231 --> 00:19:00,036
(A call from his daughter, a big fan of the GBRB series)

470
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:01,729
- Hello?
- Hello, Ra On.

471
00:19:01,730 --> 00:19:02,800
This is Uncle Kyung Soo.

472
00:19:04,970 --> 00:19:06,470
- Really?
- Yes.

473
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:07,970
Gosh, this is unbelievable.

474
00:19:09,010 --> 00:19:11,040
I just cleaned up horse manure...

475
00:19:11,470 --> 00:19:12,579
with your father.

476
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:15,479
(I cleaned up horse manure.)

477
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,680
I've cleaned up a lot of it too.

478
00:19:18,850 --> 00:19:19,880
That makes us comrades.

479
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:21,450
Comrades.

480
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:22,549
(He finds another horse manure enthusiast.)

481
00:19:22,550 --> 00:19:26,419
I've watched all the GBRB series.

482
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:27,490
Really?

483
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,060
- Yes.
- Wait.

484
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:31,290
Here's the tall person.

485
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:33,899
(The tall person is waiting.)

486
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:34,960
Hello, Ra On.

487
00:19:35,370 --> 00:19:36,929
Gosh, hello.

488
00:19:36,930 --> 00:19:39,600
(She's so cute.)

489
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:41,369
Ra On, this is Uncle Kwang Soo.

490
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:42,869
Oh, my. This is so amazing.

491
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:44,969
(The CEO's daughter is a human reaction machine.)

492
00:19:44,970 --> 00:19:46,009
Are you being honest?

493
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:47,609
Do you really find it amazing?

494
00:19:47,610 --> 00:19:51,179
- It sounds like you're faking it.
- Of course not. It's very amazing.

495
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,680
- She's so cute.
- Tell me more.

496
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:56,249
I'm not just saying this. I've watched a ton of your movies.

497
00:19:56,250 --> 00:19:57,990
Really? Which ones?

498
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,859
I've seen "Tazza" and...

499
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:02,190
But that's R-rated.

500
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:04,060
How...

501
00:20:04,530 --> 00:20:06,400
Ra On, how are you already watching that?

502
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,730
- Anyway...
- I mean...

503
00:20:08,970 --> 00:20:11,070
Is there anything you'd like from us?

504
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:13,370
- Something you want to say...
- What I'd like?

505
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:18,509
Have a good time during your stay.

506
00:20:18,510 --> 00:20:20,140
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

507
00:20:20,340 --> 00:20:21,340
She's cute.

508
00:20:22,010 --> 00:20:24,450
If she asked me for allowance, I'd want to give her some.

509
00:20:25,050 --> 00:20:26,379
- You're adorable.
- Are you serious?

510
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,380
No...

511
00:20:27,381 --> 00:20:29,089
(Pure innocence)

512
00:20:29,090 --> 00:20:30,090
Ra On,

513
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:31,450
I was just saying.

514
00:20:31,850 --> 00:20:32,990
Oh, I see.

515
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:35,289
What was that? "Oh, I see?"

516
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:37,289
Ra On, here's your dad on the phone.

517
00:20:37,290 --> 00:20:39,829
- Hold on.
- Okay.

518
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:42,270
Finish your exams well.

519
00:20:43,070 --> 00:20:46,099
- Okay? I love you.
- He dotes on his daughter.

520
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:48,300
- I feel really left out.
- Her wish came true.

521
00:20:48,870 --> 00:20:50,509
I've never seen this side of him.

522
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:52,279
(The ranch owner who's sweet only to horses and his daughter)

523
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:55,610
(A clear fish soup arrives to finish off the meal.)

524
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:57,880
(Slurping)

525
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:58,980
It tastes good.

526
00:21:01,990 --> 00:21:03,189
It's like beef and radish soup.

527
00:21:03,190 --> 00:21:05,230
(The exhaustion from a hard day's work melts away.)

528
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:11,129
The clear soup was the best.

529
00:21:11,130 --> 00:21:12,299
The clear soup.

530
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:13,699
I'm full...

531
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:15,869
up to here. I'm really full.

532
00:21:15,870 --> 00:21:17,069
All the food is served, right?

533
00:21:17,070 --> 00:21:18,229
Yes.

534
00:21:18,230 --> 00:21:19,400
After using the restroom...

535
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:21,469
- We'll set it up right away.
