00:44:55,050 --> 00:44:56,650
- Fish?
- "Parasite?"

1325
00:44:57,120 --> 00:44:58,120
- "Parasite?" - Frog...

1326
00:44:58,120 --> 00:44:59,120
Okay!

1327
00:45:00,790 --> 00:45:03,020
(Next question)

1328
00:45:03,290 --> 00:45:04,659
("The Admiral: Roaring Currents")

1329
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,760
Yi Sun Sin! "The Admiral: Roaring Currents."

1330
00:45:07,030 --> 00:45:08,030
(Yi Sun Sin!)

1331
00:45:08,031 --> 00:45:09,059
("The Admiral: Roaring Currents")

1332
00:45:09,060 --> 00:45:10,369
Okay.

1333
00:45:10,370 --> 00:45:12,050
(An immediate answer at Admiral Yi's pose)

1334
00:45:12,170 --> 00:45:14,039
(Next question)

1335
00:45:14,040 --> 00:45:15,369
(Rectangular)

1336
00:45:15,370 --> 00:45:16,370
TV?

1337
00:45:16,371 --> 00:45:17,909
- "Taegukgi." - "Taegukgi."

1338
00:45:17,910 --> 00:45:19,169
("Taegukgi")

1339
00:45:19,170 --> 00:45:20,279
Okay!

1340
00:45:20,280 --> 00:45:22,110
Let's go. We must hurry!

1341
00:45:23,310 --> 00:45:25,410
(Get 1 more question right, and it's a 9-9 tie.)

1342
00:45:26,380 --> 00:45:27,519
Hurry!

1343
00:45:27,520 --> 00:45:28,600
(There's enough time left.)

1344
00:45:29,720 --> 00:45:31,519
- You stabbed someone.
- "Friend."

1345
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:33,460
Let's go. We must hurry!

1346
00:45:34,960 --> 00:45:36,890
(Next question)

1347
00:45:37,860 --> 00:45:39,790
- You stabbed someone.
- "Friend."

1348
00:45:40,530 --> 00:45:42,560
What is it? Move!

1349
00:45:42,900 --> 00:45:44,530
Achick!

1350
00:45:45,300 --> 00:45:46,999
- Move!
- Do something.

1351
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:48,570
You stabbed someone? What is it?

1352
00:45:48,700 --> 00:45:50,946
- At least the letter.
- One letter. What's the first one?

1353
00:45:50,970 --> 00:45:52,709
(Sung Joon is silent.)

1354
00:45:52,710 --> 00:45:54,609
(Everyone)

1355
00:45:54,610 --> 00:45:56,509
(The silence drags on.)

1356
00:45:56,510 --> 00:45:58,550
Answer me! What's the first letter?

1357
00:45:59,150 --> 00:46:00,619
(Sung Joon is still silent.)

1358
00:46:00,620 --> 00:46:02,619
- One letter each.
- Pass.

1359
00:46:02,620 --> 00:46:04,220
- You can't pass anymore.
- Oh, no.

1360
00:46:04,550 --> 00:46:05,949
- You can't.
- Hurry. Please!

1361
00:46:05,950 --> 00:46:07,389
- Please!
- Do something!

1362
00:46:07,390 --> 00:46:09,519
- Please do something!
- Please.

1363
00:46:09,520 --> 00:46:10,729
Weren't you competitive?

1364
00:46:10,730 --> 00:46:12,129
Please do something.

1365
00:46:12,130 --> 00:46:14,030
What are you doing? Hurry up and move!

1366
00:46:14,360 --> 00:46:15,529
Fifteen seconds left.

1367
00:46:15,530 --> 00:46:16,530
What...

1368
00:46:16,531 --> 00:46:18,630
(Not much time is left.)

1369
00:46:18,730 --> 00:46:19,829
Move!

1370
00:46:19,830 --> 00:46:21,039
- Quiet. Hush.
- Knife?

1371
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:22,299
(He's moving!)

1372
00:46:22,300 --> 00:46:23,770
- Mountain?
- House?

1373
00:46:24,210 --> 00:46:26,709
(Another square?)

1374
00:46:26,710 --> 00:46:28,540
What's that? Even Kim Woo Bin was that.

1375
00:46:29,180 --> 00:46:31,410
What in the world is it? A square?

1376
00:46:32,350 --> 00:46:33,350
Is it an action movie?

1377
00:46:33,351 --> 00:46:34,719
- Knife. He stabbed someone.
- What is it?

1378
00:46:34,720 --> 00:46:35,720
He stabbed someone.

1379
00:46:35,721 --> 00:46:37,190
- Who?
- What did you stab?

1380
00:46:37,390 --> 00:46:38,620
There are too many like that.

1381
00:46:39,820 --> 00:46:40,820
Time over!

1382
00:46:41,090 --> 00:46:42,090
The end!

1383
00:46:43,990 --> 00:46:45,530
("The Outlaws")

1384
00:46:46,690 --> 00:46:48,800
(Sighing)

1385
00:46:57,510 --> 00:47:01,510
- Were you drawing a city with this?
- Yes.

1386
00:47:02,210 --> 00:47:04,450
(The truth behind the square)

1387
00:47:06,380 --> 00:47:07,380
Listen.

1388
00:47:08,150 --> 00:47:09,380
If both Kim Woo Bin...

1389
00:47:09,650 --> 00:47:10,950
and the city were this...

1390
00:47:11,650 --> 00:47:13,560
How were we supposed to guess from it?

1391
00:47:15,760 --> 00:47:17,429
(Kim)

1392
00:47:17,430 --> 00:47:20,130
(City)

1393
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:22,860
Why keep drawing squares when nobody can guess?

1394
00:47:23,260 --> 00:47:24,699
Kyung Soo has lost himself.

1395
00:47:24,700 --> 00:47:26,729
(Team KKPP has lost.)

1396
00:47:26,730 --> 00:47:27,739
It was tough.

1397
00:47:27,740 --> 00:47:29,139
Mow the grass,

1398
00:47:29,140 --> 00:47:30,609
pay for dinner,

1399
00:47:30,610 --> 00:47:33,340
and even get 30 sacks of feed.

1400
00:47:34,180 --> 00:47:35,879
(What's the reason behind losing?)

1401
00:47:35,880 --> 00:47:36,880
Well...

1402
00:47:37,210 --> 00:47:38,380
Our teamwork...

1403
00:47:39,080 --> 00:47:40,080
was lacking.

1404
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:42,050
- The teamwork?
- Yes.

1405
00:47:42,650 --> 00:47:44,150
(Our teamwork...)

1406
00:47:45,250 --> 00:47:47,189
(Looking around)

1407
00:47:47,190 --> 00:47:48,620
I'm getting goosebumps.

1408
00:47:49,720 --> 00:47:51,060
We had great teamwork.

1409
00:47:51,660 --> 00:47:53,390
Sung Joon is really scary.

1410
00:47:54,160 --> 00:47:56,800
(Anything you want to say to Sung Joon?)

1411
00:47:58,930 --> 00:48:03,000
(Answering with a square that Sung Joon loves)

1412
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:05,740
But still, I could've done better.

1413
00:48:06,470 --> 00:48:08,790
I feel a little bad that I wasn't able to express it well.

1414
00:48:09,280 --> 00:48:12,080
(He's actually feeling really bad.)

1415
00:48:12,550 --> 00:48:14,020
One, two, three.

1416
00:48:14,750 --> 00:48:16,879
- Good.
- Well done.

1417
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:17,889
Well done.

1418
00:48:17,890 --> 00:48:18,919
(After the fruitless dinner)

1419
00:48:18,920 --> 00:48:19,920
Well done.

1420
00:48:19,920 --> 00:48:20,920
(Cheering him up)

1421
00:48:22,060 --> 00:48:24,060
- I paid for it.
- Give me your account number.

1422
00:48:24,560 --> 00:48:26,289
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

1423
00:48:26,290 --> 00:48:27,300
Let's go.

1424
00:48:28,530 --> 00:48:30,129
Thank you, Sung Joon.

1425
00:48:30,130 --> 00:48:31,499
Get home safely.

1426
00:48:31,500 --> 00:48:32,770
(They arrived at their house.)

1427
00:48:33,470 --> 00:48:35,670
(Current time: 11:30pm)

1428
00:48:35,870 --> 00:48:37,109
Good night.

1429
00:48:37,110 --> 00:48:38,570
- Good night.
- Good night.

1430
00:48:39,610 --> 00:48:42,340
(The trainees go straight to bed from fatigue.)

1431
00:48:43,680 --> 00:48:46,480
(After a tiresome day, )

1432
00:48:47,520 --> 00:48:51,150
(the last morning of the training has come.)

1433
00:48:51,620 --> 00:48:53,960
(Kwang Soo who got up early)

1434
00:48:55,360 --> 00:48:56,589
(Slapping)

1435
00:48:56,590 --> 00:48:57,590
Yes?

1436
00:48:57,960 --> 00:48:58,989
(Slapping)

1437
00:48:58,990 --> 00:48:59,990
Yes?

1438
00:49:00,230 --> 00:49:04,099
(Waking up Kyung Soo with love yet again)

1439
00:49:04,100 --> 00:49:05,799
- Go wash up.
- What?

1440
00:49:05,800 --> 00:49:06,870
Go wash up.

1441
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:09,800
(Silence)

1442
00:49:11,070 --> 00:49:12,739
(Confiscating his blanket)

1443
00:49:12,740 --> 00:49:14,740
The alarm hasn't gone off yet.

1444
00:49:16,540 --> 00:49:21,750
(Regardless, Kwang Soo even opens the window.)

1445
00:49:23,420 --> 00:49:27,660
(Kyung Soo wakes up by force.)

1446
00:49:29,220 --> 00:49:32,460
(But Kwang Soo...)

1447
00:49:37,100 --> 00:49:38,130
(Laughing)

1448
00:49:40,100 --> 00:49:45,040
(He's satisfied only after taking Kyung Soo to the bathroom.)

1449
00:49:45,340 --> 00:49:48,540
(After washing up, it's time to put on sunscreen.)

1450
00:49:49,540 --> 00:49:51,050
Is this really sunscreen?

1451
00:49:52,750 --> 00:49:54,520
It feels like regular cream.

1452
00:49:55,620 --> 00:50:00,390
(Taking a vivid shot of Kyung Soo applying sunscreen)

1453
00:50:00,690 --> 00:50:02,859
The sunscreen leaves no white residue.

1454
00:50:02,860 --> 00:50:03,959
No, right?

1455
00:50:03,960 --> 00:50:05,730
It doesn't make our faces pale.

1456
00:50:06,660 --> 00:50:08,400
I applied the sunscreen earlier.

1457
00:50:10,700 --> 00:50:11,970
It's nice for reapplying.

1458
00:50:16,740 --> 00:50:17,970
It doesn't sting your eyes.

1459
00:50:20,710 --> 00:50:22,209
(Done getting ready for work)

1460
00:50:22,210 --> 00:50:23,510
Let's go if you're all done.

1461
00:50:25,180 --> 00:50:28,680
(GBRB Farm Operation - Go Go Farm)

1462
00:50:29,020 --> 00:50:30,550
When do we go to buy the feed?

1463
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:33,490
- Buying the feed is first, right?
- Yes.

1464
00:50:34,960 --> 00:50:36,689
(They must get the feed for losing yesterday's game.)

1465
00:50:36,690 --> 00:50:38,370
We could've gotten one more hour of sleep.

1466
00:50:38,960 --> 00:50:41,329
Sung Joon is already here and waiting for you.

1467
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:42,330
Really?

1468
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:46,100
(Sung Joon came to pick them up for work.)

1469
00:50:46,470 --> 00:50:47,640
Good morning, Sung Joon.

1470
00:50:47,870 --> 00:50:49,700
Good morning.

1471
00:50:51,470 --> 00:50:54,310
(Sung Joon's face makes him recall yesterday's square.)

1472
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:57,209
What did you think before bed last night? What crossed your mind?

1473
00:50:57,210 --> 00:50:58,480
I'm genuinely curious.

1474
00:50:58,710 --> 00:51:00,210
Today was meaningful.

1475
00:51:00,680 --> 00:51:02,280
- Meaningful?
- Yes.

1476
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:04,550
What part of it was meaningful?

1477
00:51:05,790 --> 00:51:07,689
- Well...
- Was it fun?

1478
00:51:07,690 --> 00:51:08,989
Yes, exactly.

1479
00:51:08,990 --> 00:51:10,560
It's all good as long as it was fun.

1480
00:51:11,330 --> 00:51:12,330
- Let's hit the road.
- Okay.

1481
00:51:12,331 --> 00:51:13,360
Okay.

1482
00:51:18,300 --> 00:51:19,500
Good morning, sir.

1483
00:51:19,870 --> 00:51:21,369
- Good morning.
- Did you sleep well?

1484
00:51:21,370 --> 00:51:22,799
- Yes.
- Did you have a good night?

1485
00:51:22,800 --> 00:51:24,846
(The feed delivery task will be in the bonus footage.)

1486
00:51:24,870 --> 00:51:26,939
- Were there no orders from the app?
- Sorry?

1487
00:51:26,940 --> 00:51:28,300
Were there no orders from the app?

1488
00:51:28,510 --> 00:51:29,540
No.

1489
00:51:29,940 --> 00:51:31,580
- What a bummer.
- I doubt we'll get any.

1490
00:51:31,880 --> 00:51:34,426
(Starting the day fresh by asking about the manure order status)

1491
00:51:34,450 --> 00:51:36,119
We've got another task to do,

1492
00:51:36,120 --> 00:51:37,219
- so unload them.
- Okay.

1493
00:51:37,220 --> 00:51:38,690
- Unload them separately.
- Got it.

1494
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:39,989
- Keep it up.
- Okay.

1495
00:51:39,990 --> 00:51:41,119
- Understood.
- Yes, sir.

1496
00:51:41,120 --> 00:51:42,389
Having many workers is great.

1497
00:51:42,390 --> 00:51:43,460
Good.

1498
00:51:43,760 --> 00:51:44,760
I find it comforting.

1499
00:51:47,500 --> 00:51:48,630
Maybe we're out of it.

1500
00:51:49,160 --> 00:51:50,929
- The salt...
- How cute! The foal is so cute!

1501
00:51:50,930 --> 00:51:51,969
The foal.

1502
00:51:51,970 --> 00:51:53,610
- The foal looks happy.
- It has escaped.

1503
00:51:53,700 --> 00:51:55,099
- Why is it there?
- I know, right?

1504
00:51:55,100 --> 00:51:58,470
(Spotted Gofarm outside the fence)

1505
00:51:58,740 --> 00:52:00,009
- Look at it all happy.
- Don't we have to transfer...

1506
00:52:00,010 --> 00:52:01,310
It's all happy.

1507
00:52:01,440 --> 00:52:04,010
I don't think it even realizes it's outside the fence.

1508
00:52:04,210 --> 00:52:05,530
I think it'll go over right away.

1509
00:52:06,150 --> 00:52:07,320
Yes, there it goes.

1510
00:52:07,920 --> 00:52:08,979
(Stuck)

1511
00:52:08,980 --> 00:52:10,550
Oh, no. Duck deeper.

1512
00:52:11,450 --> 00:52:12,520
Well done.

1513
00:52:12,850 --> 00:52:13,960
So adorable.

1514
00:52:15,760 --> 00:52:17,859
(As expected of my baby.)

1515
00:52:17,860 --> 00:52:19,790
What's this? I feel the pressure.

1516
00:52:20,130 --> 00:52:21,970
Are they watching us because the food is here?

1517
00:52:23,300 --> 00:52:24,970
This is a bit much.

1518
00:52:25,730 --> 00:52:27,640
- That one's sleeping on the ground.
- Where?

1519
00:52:28,670 --> 00:52:30,670
- It must feel at ease.
- Exactly.

1520
00:52:30,810 --> 00:52:32,910
So horses don't actually sleep standing up.

1521
00:52:33,470 --> 00:52:35,139
I thought they slept standing up.

1522
00:52:35,140 --> 00:52:37,309
(While enjoying the morning at the ranch, )

1523
00:52:37,310 --> 00:52:39,980
(they start working on a fresh note.)

1524
00:52:40,620 --> 00:52:42,150
The feed has to be unloaded, right?

1525
00:52:42,950 --> 00:52:45,819
(The feed from this morning has to be unloaded first.)

1526
00:52:45,820 --> 00:52:47,889
Yes, but the car needs to be backed up first.

1527
00:52:47,890 --> 00:52:49,820
(But this car needs to be moved first.)

1528
00:52:50,160 --> 00:52:51,659
I'll back up that truck.

1529
00:52:51,660 --> 00:52:52,729
Okay.

1530
00:52:52,730 --> 00:52:55,730
(Kwang Soo is going to back up the feed truck.)

1531
00:52:56,330 --> 00:52:59,930
(Trying to back up the truck)

1532
00:53:03,470 --> 00:53:06,570
(Something is wrong.)

1533
00:53:07,110 --> 00:53:09,010
(Backing up again)

1534
00:53:09,080 --> 00:53:10,239
But it's in reverse.

1535
00:53:10,240 --> 00:53:11,280
(Going forward)

1536
00:53:11,450 --> 00:53:12,450
(Moving)

1537
00:53:12,451 --> 00:53:14,520
- Where are you going?
- It's...

1538
00:53:16,220 --> 00:53:17,790
I put the gear in reverse.

1539
00:53:18,420 --> 00:53:19,420
(The truck moves forward in reverse.)

1540
00:53:19,420 --> 00:53:20,420
Is it moving forward?

1541
00:53:22,660 --> 00:53:23,960
- I've got it.
- Here he comes.

1542
00:53:24,290 --> 00:53:28,500
(Thankfully, he's gotten the hang of it fast.)

1543
00:53:28,730 --> 00:53:30,130
Those are really heavy.

1544
00:53:31,100 --> 00:53:32,330
This looks tough.

1545
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:34,100
- Hurry up.
- I'll do it.

1546
00:53:34,500 --> 00:53:35,539
No, wait.

1547
00:53:35,540 --> 00:53:37,040
(Tossing one after the other)

1548
00:53:38,210 --> 00:53:39,639
(Hunched)

1549
00:53:39,640 --> 00:53:41,539
(The position looks really uncomfortable.)

1550
00:53:41,540 --> 00:53:42,739
This should do.

1551
00:53:42,740 --> 00:53:44,380
(Bending down was hard on Kwang Soo.)

1552
00:53:46,850 --> 00:53:50,690
- In front of...
- Take out...

1553
00:53:51,550 --> 00:53:52,550
(Sliding)

1554
00:53:52,551 --> 00:53:54,390
It's a little...

1555
00:53:56,590 --> 00:53:59,460
(His view from behind isn't all that nice.)

1556
00:54:00,390 --> 00:54:01,999
Why are you handing it over like this?

1557
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:03,000
This is the best...

1558
00:54:03,730 --> 00:54:05,090
It doesn't strain my back as much.

1559
00:54:06,670 --> 00:54:07,976
It also seems to be the most efficient.

1560
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:09,000
I see.

1561
00:54:09,240 --> 00:54:10,640
I'm sorry, Ye Eun. I really am.

1562
00:54:11,970 --> 00:54:15,410
(Will you accept my apology?)

1563
00:54:17,010 --> 00:54:21,150
(After the tough time for everyone)

1564
00:54:21,980 --> 00:54:23,050
The last one.

1565
00:54:24,250 --> 00:54:27,390
(The last sack is off the truck.)

1566
00:54:27,490 --> 00:54:29,720
- We need to load these, right?
- The oats as well.

1567
00:54:30,830 --> 00:54:31,890
How many do we load?

1568
00:54:32,090 --> 00:54:33,830
- One is enough.
- One?

1569
00:54:34,630 --> 00:54:37,000
(Packed the oats that will be given out with the feed)

1570
00:54:38,230 --> 00:54:39,299
- I'm closing the door.
- Okay.

1571
00:54:39,300 --> 00:54:40,500
(Off to give the food)

1572
00:54:41,540 --> 00:54:44,969
(Kyung Soo takes a look at the work phone.)

1573
00:54:44,970 --> 00:54:46,109
Wait a minute.

1574
00:54:46,110 --> 00:54:47,540
Wait a minute!

1575
00:54:48,540 --> 00:54:49,639
(He spotted something?)

1576
00:54:49,640 --> 00:54:50,750
- Hold on!
- What is it?

1577
00:54:52,250 --> 00:54:53,279
It's here!

1578
00:54:53,280 --> 00:54:55,950
- What did they say?
- They asked if it's available.

1579
00:54:56,680 --> 00:54:59,119
(The long-awaited manure order is here.)

1580
00:54:59,120 --> 00:55:00,120
How heavy is one sack?

1581
00:55:00,121 --> 00:55:01,321
Wait. I need to reply to them.

1582
00:55:01,790 --> 00:55:03,559
We've got an order!

1583
00:55:03,560 --> 00:55:05,359
(The 1st order came in after 3 days of worrying.)

1584
00:55:05,360 --> 00:55:06,590
Don't sound as if...

1585
00:55:06,690 --> 00:55:08,029
"Is it available? How heavy is one sack?"

1586
00:55:08,030 --> 00:55:09,860
- Isn't it 20kg per sack?
- Correct.

1587
00:55:10,900 --> 00:55:14,640
(Sending a reply first)

1588
00:55:15,470 --> 00:55:16,470
Didn't you get one?

1589
00:55:16,600 --> 00:55:17,640
No.

1590
00:55:18,410 --> 00:55:20,539
(Feeling as if he's beaten Sung Joon)

1591
00:55:20,540 --> 00:55:21,956
- Do you need advice?
- The winner's smile.

1592
00:55:21,980 --> 00:55:24,309
- If you reduce it by 50 cents...
- I see.

1593
00:55:24,310 --> 00:55:25,409
- The load...
- Don't write anything like...

1594
00:55:25,410 --> 00:55:26,550
"Jack and the Beanstalk."

1595
00:55:26,710 --> 00:55:27,779
Move to business talk.

1596
00:55:27,780 --> 00:55:29,950
(The trainees finally have a taste of success.)

1597
00:55:30,750 --> 00:55:31,789
(Waiting for the buyer's reply)

1598
00:55:31,790 --> 00:55:33,049
Don't sound as if you were waiting...

1599
00:55:33,050 --> 00:55:34,319
- for an order.
- One sack...

1600
00:55:34,320 --> 00:55:35,819
- is 10kg, right?
- Then how?

1601
00:55:35,820 --> 00:55:37,059
- Play mind games.
- How?

1602
00:55:37,060 --> 00:55:38,329
- Ask how much they need.
- Play mind games?

1603
00:55:38,330 --> 00:55:40,960
- We shouldn't play mind games.
- Ask, "How much do you need?"

1604
00:55:41,630 --> 00:55:43,199
Leave that chat room,

1605
00:55:43,200 --> 00:55:44,269
- or they'll know you've read it.
- Right.

1606
00:55:44,270 --> 00:55:45,670
Leave the chat room already.

1607
00:55:46,300 --> 00:55:47,369
Why?

1608
00:55:47,370 --> 00:55:48,499
Replying immediately looks desperate.

1609
00:55:48,500 --> 00:55:50,369
A quick reply is important...

1610
00:55:50,370 --> 00:55:52,109
- in Korea.
- But you look desperate to sell.

1611
00:55:52,110 --> 00:55:53,569
Exactly. For days...

1612
00:55:53,570 --> 00:55:54,639
Showing how rich the manure is...

1613
00:55:54,640 --> 00:55:56,209
This isn't the time for that.

1614
00:55:56,210 --> 00:55:58,979
- What if they change their mind?
- Stop with the nonsense.

1615
00:55:58,980 --> 00:56:00,919
- Speed matters.
- "This guy is desperate."

1616
00:56:00,920 --> 00:56:03,379
- "Something must be mixed in it." - What?

1617
00:56:03,380 --> 00:56:04,749
- They might get the wrong idea.
- He's right.

1618
00:56:04,750 --> 00:56:06,019
- From the message?
- Yes.

1619
00:56:06,020 --> 00:56:07,460
(Too many cooks for one reply)

1620
00:56:07,890 --> 00:56:09,890
- Did they read it?
- No, not yet.

1621
00:56:10,560 --> 00:56:12,230
Stop it. Why are you sending another one?

1622
00:56:12,760 --> 00:56:14,129
We should quickly sell one.

1623
00:56:14,130 --> 00:56:16,029
No, this is totally fine.

1624
00:56:16,030 --> 00:56:17,230
(They wait for a reply first.)

1625
00:56:19,230 --> 00:56:20,500
Where are we going right now?

1626
00:56:20,940 --> 00:56:22,769
- To go feed the horses.
- To go feed the horses.

1627
00:56:22,770 --> 00:56:24,039
But why are we taking this road?

1628
00:56:24,040 --> 00:56:27,070
The special care zone where Yeonjin is.

1629
00:56:28,010 --> 00:56:29,079
What a nice place.

1630
00:56:29,080 --> 00:56:31,410
(They arrived at the special care zone.)

1631
00:56:32,480 --> 00:56:35,850
(Where the trainees' partner horses are)

1632
00:56:36,180 --> 00:56:38,189
(They're here to give breakfast in the special care zone.)

1633
00:56:38,190 --> 00:56:40,760
(Morning Task Schedule: Special care zone feed)

1634
00:56:40,920 --> 00:56:42,120
- This horse?
- Let's go.

1635
00:56:42,620 --> 00:56:44,460
(And in the special care zone...)

1636
00:56:44,690 --> 00:56:46,329
You're right. He's quite big.

1637
00:56:46,330 --> 00:56:47,530
He's huge.

1638
00:56:48,700 --> 00:56:50,259
He's big. You can feel him jump, right?

1639
00:56:50,260 --> 00:56:52,930
(There's Big Arthur.)

1640
00:56:53,300 --> 00:56:54,669
What about the others?

1641
00:56:54,670 --> 00:56:56,399
- I'll teach you how.
- Okay.

1642
00:56:56,400 --> 00:56:57,569
(Trying to feed Arthur first)

1643
00:56:57,570 --> 00:56:58,740
- Come here.
- Over there...

1644
00:56:59,340 --> 00:57:00,469
Or he'll eat the whole thing.

1645
00:57:00,470 --> 00:57:01,670
- No, this way.
- It's like...

1646
00:57:02,740 --> 00:57:04,550
No, stop. He's lost it.

1647
00:57:05,210 --> 00:57:07,110
Wait. How far will you follow us?

1648
00:57:07,480 --> 00:57:09,449
(Arthur chasing after them is a different story.)

1649
00:57:09,450 --> 00:57:10,549
Let's hurry.

1650
00:57:10,550 --> 00:57:12,420
Here. Wait.

1651
00:57:12,550 --> 00:57:14,720
(Pouring it in the bowl before he takes the sack)

1652
00:57:17,490 --> 00:57:18,690
Dig in.

1653
00:57:20,490 --> 00:57:24,199
(Kwang Soo pours in a generous amount.)

1654
00:57:24,200 --> 00:57:25,369
Rip it. Rip the opening.

1655
00:57:25,370 --> 00:57:26,570
- Is this a new one?
- Yes.

1656
00:57:26,670 --> 00:57:29,700
(Meanwhile, the intern opens the oat sack.)

1657
00:57:30,740 --> 00:57:32,210
Has it always been this color?

1658
00:57:33,370 --> 00:57:34,380
- Dig in.
- What's this?

1659
00:57:35,410 --> 00:57:36,479
Sung Joon.

1660
00:57:36,480 --> 00:57:39,309
- Yes?
- How much do we give?

1661
00:57:39,310 --> 00:57:40,479
Oats...

1662
00:57:40,480 --> 00:57:42,719
But there are red beans, not oats. Is that okay?

1663
00:57:42,720 --> 00:57:43,720
What red beans?

1664
00:57:43,721 --> 00:57:44,750
- This one.
- It's red.

1665
00:57:46,190 --> 00:57:48,120
Are these beans?

1666
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:51,230
- There are no oats.
- We brought the wrong one.

1667
00:57:54,860 --> 00:57:56,499
It... We brought the wrong one.

1668
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:58,070
- So what is that?
- Sorry?

1669
00:57:58,870 --> 00:58:01,600
I think we brought seeds.

1670
00:58:02,470 --> 00:58:05,040
(Anyone can tell they are not oats.)

1671
00:58:05,140 --> 00:58:06,640
What are you saying?

1672
00:58:06,970 --> 00:58:08,310
We need to bring oats.

1673
00:58:09,980 --> 00:58:11,310
(Laughing)

1674
00:58:12,010 --> 00:58:13,010
(Realizing)

1675
00:58:13,011 --> 00:58:14,691
(The blunder guy is bright today as well.)

1676
00:58:15,120 --> 00:58:16,180
Sung Joon.

1677
00:58:16,680 --> 00:58:18,600
You're the type to make extra work for yourself.

1678
00:58:19,190 --> 00:58:22,220
(Sung Joon ends up leaving to get oats.)

1679
00:58:22,660 --> 00:58:24,230
- Let's feed the others.
- For now...

1680
00:58:25,260 --> 00:58:26,459
- Shall we?
- Yes.

1681
00:58:26,460 --> 00:58:28,060
(Feeding the other horses while waiting)

1682
00:58:28,500 --> 00:58:29,500
Morris.

1683
00:58:30,030 --> 00:58:32,329
(First is Morris, Kyung Soo's partner.)

1684
00:58:32,330 --> 00:58:33,970
Morris, you rolled in the dirt again.

1685
00:58:34,800 --> 00:58:36,199
He's gotten dark.

1686
00:58:36,200 --> 00:58:37,300
(Dirty in a day)

1687
00:58:37,770 --> 00:58:38,940
Time to eat, Morris.

1688
00:58:39,640 --> 00:58:40,770
Morris.

1689
00:58:41,410 --> 00:58:42,410
(Give me food.)

1690
00:58:42,411 --> 00:58:43,640
No. Wait.

1691
00:58:44,510 --> 00:58:45,610
Dig in.

1692
00:58:46,110 --> 00:58:47,150
That's it.

1693
00:58:47,950 --> 00:58:49,250
Morris is clever.

1694
00:58:50,180 --> 00:58:51,890
He seems like a smart horse.

1695
00:58:53,690 --> 00:58:54,890
He's good at using his nose.

1696
00:58:57,390 --> 00:58:58,429
It's his.

1697
00:58:58,430 --> 00:59:00,189
(Morris secures his own food.)

1698
00:59:00,190 --> 00:59:01,360
Let's give food to Snow now.

1699
00:59:01,800 --> 00:59:03,376
- How do you know all their names?
- Snow!

1700
00:59:03,400 --> 00:59:05,330
(Next is John Snow, Kwang Soo's partner.)

1701
00:59:05,730 --> 00:59:07,100
Look at his soft tail.

1702
00:59:08,440 --> 00:59:09,670
Let's eat, Snow.

1703
00:59:10,940 --> 00:59:12,239
- Kwang Soo.
- Yes?

1704
00:59:12,240 --> 00:59:13,540
Isn't he Snow?

1705
00:59:13,770 --> 00:59:15,309
Which one? He hurt his leg.

1706
00:59:15,310 --> 00:59:16,480
Isn't that Snow?

1707
00:59:16,880 --> 00:59:19,280
(This is Snow.)

1708
00:59:20,550 --> 00:59:21,680
Who are you?

1709
00:59:22,320 --> 00:59:23,749
Who are you?

1710
00:59:23,750 --> 00:59:24,989
- Let's feed him first.
- Snow is over there.

1711
00:59:24,990 --> 00:59:26,489
- Let's go feed him. You're right.
- Who are you?

1712
00:59:26,490 --> 00:59:28,090
(The two horses do look alike.)

1713
00:59:29,160 --> 00:59:30,189
(Smelling)

1714
00:59:30,190 --> 00:59:31,950
It's not him. He doesn't smell like shampoo.

1715
00:59:32,460 --> 00:59:34,159
It's not Snow. He doesn't smell like shampoo.

1716
00:59:34,160 --> 00:59:35,960
(His name is Eren.)

1717
00:59:36,100 --> 00:59:37,869
Yes, this one is Snow. Hey, Snow.

1718
00:59:37,870 --> 00:59:39,030
(Happy to see Snow)

1719
00:59:40,200 --> 00:59:41,316
- All good?
- Is that enough?

1720
00:59:41,340 --> 00:59:42,620
Let's give him another scoopful.

1721
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:45,039
Dig in, okay?

1722
00:59:45,040 --> 00:59:46,569
(A generous amount for Snow as well)

1723
00:59:46,570 --> 00:59:47,740
Enjoy.

1724
00:59:48,610 --> 00:59:49,680
You're so cute.

1725
00:59:51,050 --> 00:59:52,050
Dig in.

1726
00:59:53,610 --> 00:59:55,279
It sounds delicious when you chew it.

1727
00:59:55,280 --> 00:59:57,120
(Distributing food evenly to the other horses)

1728
00:59:57,450 --> 01:00:00,790
(A delightful meal)

1729
01:00:01,790 --> 01:00:02,890
Yeonjin.

1730
01:00:03,990 --> 01:00:05,459
You're a charming one.

1731
01:00:05,460 --> 01:00:07,029
(They came to see Yeonjin last.)

1732
01:00:07,030 --> 01:00:08,130
All good?

1733
01:00:08,560 --> 01:00:09,659
Park Yeonjin!

1734
01:00:09,660 --> 01:00:11,000
- Not this one.
- No!

1735
01:00:11,100 --> 01:00:12,200
Park Yeonjin!

1736
01:00:12,930 --> 01:00:13,969
Come here.

1737
01:00:13,970 --> 01:00:14,970
(Yeonjin is scolded again.)

1738
01:00:14,970 --> 01:00:15,970
Come here.

1739
01:00:16,200 --> 01:00:20,170
(Giving out food first)

1740
01:00:20,470 --> 01:00:22,110
He's gotten quite clean.

1741
01:00:22,710 --> 01:00:24,240
Kwang Soo, his mane.

1742
01:00:24,510 --> 01:00:26,249
- His mane...
- It's like he used conditioner.

1743
01:00:26,250 --> 01:00:27,479
- Yes, it's really...
- Is that so?

1744
01:00:27,480 --> 01:00:28,549
- But why is it so...
- It looks soft.

1745
01:00:28,550 --> 01:00:29,879
He rolled in dirt yesterday.

1746
01:00:29,880 --> 01:00:30,920
(A cloud of dust)

1747
01:00:31,290 --> 01:00:32,390
How cute.

1748
01:00:33,650 --> 01:00:36,560
Scratch him ten times harder than you think.

1749
01:00:37,160 --> 01:00:38,189
(Bumping)

1750
01:00:38,190 --> 01:00:39,260
He likes it.

1751
01:00:41,330 --> 01:00:44,130
(I like you too.)

1752
01:00:44,930 --> 01:00:48,740
You know, how do I put it? The feeling of its fat is...

1753
01:00:49,500 --> 01:00:50,640
It's really nice.

1754
01:00:53,540 --> 01:00:54,610
Where are you scratching?

1755
01:00:54,840 --> 01:00:55,880
Horses like this spot.

1756
01:00:55,910 --> 01:00:57,010
That's his bottom.

1757
01:00:57,380 --> 01:00:58,979
He can't reach all the way here.

1758
01:00:58,980 --> 01:01:00,656
(She spots Kwang Soo scratching the horse's bottom.)

1759
01:01:00,680 --> 01:01:02,879
Isn't it funny to scratch the horse's bottom?

1760
01:01:02,880 --> 01:01:04,450
It's a horse,

1761
01:01:05,490 --> 01:01:07,250
but his bottom is very much like ours.

1762
01:01:08,660 --> 01:01:10,620
- That's true.
- It feels like a real butt.

1763
01:01:11,530 --> 01:01:12,929
- Is this right?
- Can we do this?

1764
01:01:12,930 --> 01:01:14,629
(Horses love it when you scratch the spot under their tail...)

1765
01:01:14,630 --> 01:01:15,829
It feels strange.

1766
01:01:15,830 --> 01:01:17,006
(that they can't reach themselves.)

1767
01:01:17,030 --> 01:01:18,030
It's a real butt.

1768
01:01:18,031 --> 01:01:19,629
I know. Come here.

1769
01:01:19,630 --> 01:01:21,550
I didn't expect it to be so similar to our butt.

1770
01:01:22,640 --> 01:01:23,640
Here?

1771
01:01:23,641 --> 01:01:25,640
- Inside here.
- Scratch his butt.

1772
01:01:26,010 --> 01:01:27,010
Right here.

1773
01:01:28,410 --> 01:01:29,440
Sung Joon.

1774
01:01:30,680 --> 01:01:32,449
You're making us work twice.

1775
01:01:32,450 --> 01:01:33,549
Goodness.

1776
01:01:33,550 --> 01:01:35,470
(Sung Joon returns after going to get the oats.)

1777
01:01:35,880 --> 01:01:37,279
(Finishing up feeding the oats)

1778
01:01:37,280 --> 01:01:38,450
Yeonjin.

1779
01:01:39,250 --> 01:01:40,919
We should've mixed it into the feed.

1780
01:01:40,920 --> 01:01:41,989
It's bibimbap,

1781
01:01:41,990 --> 01:01:43,830
but we're giving them bean sprouts separately.

1782
01:01:44,960 --> 01:01:46,060
Sung Joon, why...

1783
01:01:47,090 --> 01:01:49,559
- Kwang Soo, don't carry it around.
- What?

1784
01:01:49,560 --> 01:01:50,629
Don't carry it around.

1785
01:01:50,630 --> 01:01:51,906
- Fill it up completely.
- What is it?

1786
01:01:51,930 --> 01:01:52,930
Completely.

1787
01:01:52,931 --> 01:01:54,246
(Kyung Soo transfers the oats into his scoop.)

1788
01:01:54,270 --> 01:01:55,616
Kwang Soo, just feed the other two.

1789
01:01:55,640 --> 01:01:56,640
Okay.

1790
01:01:56,641 --> 01:01:58,241
(They plan to split and feed them fast.)

1791
01:01:59,040 --> 01:02:00,070
Have some oats.

1792
01:02:01,910 --> 01:02:03,410
- That should be enough.
- Wait.

1793
01:02:03,510 --> 01:02:05,079
He lifted it so easily.

1794
01:02:05,080 --> 01:02:06,250
- He threw it.
- Kyung Soo.

1795
01:02:07,480 --> 01:02:08,549
Did you feed him?

1796
01:02:08,550 --> 01:02:10,230
- Did we feed them all?
- We fed them all.

1797
01:02:11,190 --> 01:02:12,719
I told him to stop carrying that around.

1798
01:02:12,720 --> 01:02:14,250
Why does he keep carrying it?

1799
01:02:14,620 --> 01:02:16,260
We only need to give three handfuls.

1800
01:02:16,460 --> 01:02:19,290
Why do they keep carrying around that 20kg bag?

1801
01:02:20,060 --> 01:02:21,500
I don't understand why.

1802
01:02:21,600 --> 01:02:24,530
(It does seem heavy.)

1803
01:02:24,670 --> 01:02:25,750
Shouldn't we give him more?

1804
01:02:26,100 --> 01:02:27,629
We should give some more to Arthur.

1805
01:02:27,630 --> 01:02:29,370
- Give some more to Arthur.
- Okay.

1806
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:31,040
Oats?

1807
01:02:31,910 --> 01:02:34,140
(The oat sack she's been carrying around all this time)

1808
01:02:34,880 --> 01:02:36,710
(Sliding down)

1809
01:02:37,340 --> 01:02:39,310
Gosh, you can't do this either.

1810
01:02:41,550 --> 01:02:43,050
Listen, you guys.

1811
01:02:43,550 --> 01:02:46,150
That weighs half of my weight.

1812
01:02:47,220 --> 01:02:49,560
Don't you know how hard it is...

1813
01:02:49,660 --> 01:02:51,020
to carry feed that weighs 25kg?

1814
01:02:52,630 --> 01:02:54,800
- Get in already.
- Okay.

1815
01:02:55,930 --> 01:02:57,529
(She may not listen to her seniors.)

1816
01:02:57,530 --> 01:02:58,530
Seriously.

1817
01:02:58,531 --> 01:03:01,199
(But it's nice to see how positive she is.)

1818
01:03:01,200 --> 01:03:03,900
(Heading out to gather fresh grass for the horses)

1819
01:03:04,510 --> 01:03:05,969
- Horses are really good...
- Yes.

1820
01:03:05,970 --> 01:03:07,439
At using their muzzles.

1821
01:03:07,440 --> 01:03:09,440
- Their muzzles?
- They pull and push their bowls.

1822
01:03:09,680 --> 01:03:11,879
Just like people, some horses are efficient workers.

1823
01:03:11,880 --> 01:03:12,910
Yes.

1824
01:03:13,480 --> 01:03:14,979
And some do the same job twice.

1825
01:03:14,980 --> 01:03:15,980
Right.

1826
01:03:16,820 --> 01:03:17,889
I'm not talking about you.

1827
01:03:17,890 --> 01:03:19,719
I'm not talking about anyone in particular.

1828
01:03:19,720 --> 01:03:20,720
Okay.

1829
01:03:20,721 --> 01:03:23,660
(It sounds like he's talking about someone.)

1830
01:03:25,060 --> 01:03:26,300
Look at how dirty my hands are.

1831
01:03:27,530 --> 01:03:28,530
Unbelievable.

1832
01:03:28,600 --> 01:03:29,600
That's poop.

1833
01:03:30,930 --> 01:03:32,399
You got poop under your fingernails.

1834
01:03:32,400 --> 01:03:33,470
- Really?
- Yes.

1835
01:03:34,640 --> 01:03:36,469
You also have poop under your mouth.

1836
01:03:36,470 --> 01:03:37,470
Really?

1837
01:03:39,310 --> 01:03:41,309
- You're right.
- It's poop.

1838
01:03:41,310 --> 01:03:42,340
(Proof of her hard work)

1839
01:03:42,840 --> 01:03:44,910
Where's the tissue?

1840
01:03:45,010 --> 01:03:46,279
- Gosh.
- We got a message.

1841
01:03:46,280 --> 01:03:47,349
- We got a message.
- We got a message.

1842
01:03:47,350 --> 01:03:49,220
- We got a message.
- Where is it from?

1843
01:03:49,650 --> 01:03:50,650
Is it for us?

1844
01:03:51,350 --> 01:03:53,490
"My house is in Sagye-ri, Andeok-myeon."

